% HYBRID DYNAMICS
% ---------------------------------------------------------------
\subsection{Hybrid Dynamical Substrate (COSE)}

The proof-state vector $X(t)$ evolves under hybrid dynamics:

\begin{equation}
\frac{dX}{dt}
= S \cdot v(X,p)
+ \sum_{k} v_k \, a_k(X) \circ dP_k(t),
\label{eq:methods_hybrid}
\end{equation}

where:

\begin{itemize}
    \item $S$ is the structural dependency matrix,
    \item $v(X,p)$ is the continuous drift vector,
    \item $v_k$ are discrete event vectors,
    \item $a_k(X)$ are event propensities,
    \item $dP_k(t)$ are Poisson increments.
\end{itemize}

Continuous kinetics follow Michaelis–Menten or Hill formulations, while
discrete events encode logical transitions, contradiction triggers, and
capsule resonance interactions.

