% LYAPUNOV FUNCTIONAL
% ---------------------------------------------------------------
\subsection{Lyapunov Stability Functional}

The composite Lyapunov functional is defined as:

\begin{equation}
\mathcal{V}(X)
= (X - X^\star)^\top Q (X - X^\star)
+ \sum_{k} D_{\mathrm{KL}}\!\left(
\pi_k(X) \,\big\|\, \pi_k^\star
\right),
\label{eq:methods_lyap}
\end{equation}

with $Q \succ 0$.  
This functional detects contradictions via instability:

\begin{equation}
\dot{\mathcal{V}}(X) > 0
\quad \Rightarrow \quad
\text{Reject proof-state}.
\end{equation}

This mechanism is integrated directly into the PVP acceptance predicate.

