\subsection{Automated Theorem Proving (ATP)}

The ATP kernel verifies each inference step of a candidate proof $\Pi$
against the axiom set $\mathcal{A}$ and inference rules $\mathcal{R}$.

The ATP acceptance predicate is:

\begin{equation}
\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{ATP}}(\Pi, \psi) = 1
\quad \Longleftrightarrow \quad
\Pi \text{ is a valid derivation of } \psi.
\end{equation}

ATP ensures logical soundness independent of dynamical or cryptographic
layers.

