\subsection{Zero-Knowledge SNARK Verification}

The verified proof $\Pi$ is encoded into a succinct non-interactive
argument of knowledge (SNARK).  
Let $\kappa$ denote the security parameter.  
The soundness error satisfies:

\begin{equation}
\epsilon_{\mathrm{ZKP}} \leq 2^{-\kappa}.
\end{equation}

The SNARK layer ensures:

\begin{itemize}
    \item correctness without revealing internal proof-state data,
    \item verifier independence from COSE dynamics,
    \item cryptographic immutability.
\end{itemize}

