\subsection{Codex Capsule Commitment}

A Codex Capsule is defined as:

\begin{equation}
\mathcal{C}
= (\mathcal{M}, H_{\mathrm{commit}}, \Gamma),
\end{equation}

where $\mathcal{M}$ is the manuscript payload,
$H_{\mathrm{commit}}$ the cryptographic commitment,
and $\Gamma$ the glyph-seal semantic layer.

The commitment hash is:

\begin{equation}
H_{\mathrm{commit}}
= \mathrm{SHA256}(\mathcal{M} \parallel t \parallel \mathrm{author}),
\end{equation}

ensuring immutability and provenance integrity.

